# count-signals: question-sentence words that signal the count direction.
# format — word: direction
# readable via: shabda "count-signals" "word"
#
# these appear in the QUESTION sentence ("how many are left / in total")
# and indicate whether the asker expects a subtraction or addition result.
# distinct from common-sense-events which map EVENT verbs in premise sentences.
#
# when a question has per-grade event verbs (flew, came), those take precedence.
# these signals serve as fallback when no event verb is present in a grade,
# or as the overall question-level default direction.
#
# kshaya signals: "how many remain / are left / rest"
remaining: kshaya
left: kshaya
rest: kshaya
leftover: kshaya
#
# vriddhi signals: "how many in total / altogether"
total: vriddhi
altogether: vriddhi
combined: vriddhi
together: vriddhi
both: vriddhi
